(O113 - Quick Tool Change + Probe + Resume)
(Simplified auto tool change for use inside G-code programs.)
(Call immediately after T# M6 in your program:)
(  T2 M6)
(  O113 call [2])
(This probes the new tool and resumes with correct offset.)
(Requires: [TOOL_SETTER] X, Y, VEL, REF_Z, MAX_PROBE_DEPTH in INI)
(Requires: [PROBE] Z_SAFE in INI)

O113 sub

    #<tool_num> = #1
    #<setter_x> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]X>
    #<setter_y> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]Y>
    #<setter_vel> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]VEL>
    #<setter_ref_z> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]REF_Z>
    #<max_depth> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]MAX_PROBE_DEPTH>
    #<z_safe> = #<_ini[PROBE]Z_SAFE>

    (Save current position)
    #<saved_x> = #5420
    #<saved_y> = #5421
    #<saved_z> = #5422

    (Move to tool setter and probe)
    G90
    G53 G0 Z#<z_safe>
    G53 G0 X#<setter_x> Y#<setter_y>
    G91
    G38.2 Z[0 - #<max_depth>] F[#<setter_vel> * 4]
    G0 Z2.0
    G38.2 Z-4.0 F#<setter_vel>

    (Calculate and store tool length)
    #<tool_length> = [#5063 - #<setter_ref_z>]
    G10 L1 P#<tool_num> Z#<tool_length>
    G43 H#<tool_num>

    (Return to work position)
    G90
    G53 G0 Z#<z_safe>
    G0 X#<saved_x> Y#<saved_y>
    G0 Z#<saved_z>

    (Restart spindle at previous speed if it was running)
    (Note: M3/M4 state is preserved by LinuxCNC, so we)
    (just need to ensure the correct S word is active.)

    (MSG, Tool #<tool_num> ready. Length: #<tool_length>)

O113 endsub
M2
